    "updated_at": "2017-11-08T08:50:00Z",
    "body": "I suggested opening this as it resulted in implementer confusion and \"delays the load event\" and \"subresource\" are different enough that I think we should also have that distinction in the non-normative text. I think it's made especially confusing since \"subresource\" is a term of art. If it just listed some examples such as images and nested browsing contexts it'd be less confusing I think.",
